{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothSelection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RothSelection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothGammaProducer"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.sum_rothDegrees_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.sum_rothDegrees_le","kind":"theorem","line":291,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothSelection.lean#L291-L310","doc":"**`Σ r_h` in terms of the smallest height.**  `Σ_h rothDegrees H N h ≤ m·(log_b N + 1)` for any\n`b` below every height — because `Nat.log` is antitone in its base, so the smallest height gives\nthe largest degree.\n\nThis is the concrete form of the asymptotic `Σ r_h ≈ log N · Σ_h 1/log H_h ≤ m·log N/log H₀` that\n`hbound`'s cancellation runs on: it puts `Σ r_h` under `m·log_{H₀} N`, so the left side of the\nheight clause grows like `N^{c·m/log H₀}` against a right side of `N^p`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.exists_rothGammaFull_of_supply_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.exists_rothGammaFull_of_supply_witness","kind":"theorem","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothSelection.lean#L270-L289","doc":"**The selection machinery is applicable.**  Every hypothesis of\n`exists_rothGammaFull_of_supply` is discharged at `m = 2`, `p = q = 1`, `F = 10`, `b = 1` — the\nparameters `RothRealLadder`'s own witness uses — over the unbounded supply `Set.univ`.\n\n`hfloorExp` is the clause that pins `F`: at `m = 2` it reads `1·(1·2·5) ≤ F·1`, so `F = 10` is the\nsmallest that works, which is the same arithmetic that forced `H = 1024` in the earlier witness.\nThe two are the same constraint seen from opposite ends. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.exists_rothGammaFull_of_supply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.exists_rothGammaFull_of_supply","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothSelection.lean#L240-L268","doc":"**`Γ_m` from the supply, modulo the height clause.**  There are heights in the supply and a\nthreshold `N` such that *if* the auxiliary polynomial's height bound `b` satisfies `Γ_m`'s last\nclause for them, then all seven clauses hold.\n\nThe implication is the honest shape.  `hbound` is a statement *about the produced data*, so it\ncannot be a hypothesis of the existential — and quantifying it over all possible `H`, `N` would\ndemand far more than the argument needs.  `hbound_mono` is what makes the implication\ndischargeable: the clause improves as `H₀` grows, and the supply is unbounded.\n\n⚠ `b` is a **function** of the produced data, not a constant.  It was a constant in the first\ndraft, and that version cannot be used: the `b` this is actually applied at is\n`⌈siegelHeight (rothDegrees H N) α μ⌉`, which depends on the `H` and `N` the theorem itself\nproduces.  A constant `b` cannot be instantiated with it, so the \"honest shape\" was still the\nwrong one — honest about `hbound` and wrong about `b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.exists_heights_and_N","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.exists_heights_and_N","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothSelection.lean#L219-L238","doc":"**The data, and four of `Γ_m`'s inputs.**  From an unbounded supply of admissible heights:\n`m` of them, a threshold `N`, and the growth, floor, `two_le` and `hlarge` clauses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.hbound_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.hbound_mono","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothSelection.lean#L190-L202","doc":"**Raising `H j` never hurts `Γ_m`'s height clause**, with the degrees held fixed.  This is the\nformal content of \"choose `q₁` large\": the clause is monotone in the height, and `b` does not move\nwhen `r` does not.\n\nNo sign condition on `b` is needed — I wrote `0 ≤ b` and the linter reported it unused, which is\nright: only the *base* `H j` has to be non-negative, and it is a natural number.  The stronger\nstatement is kept. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.exists_pow_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.exists_pow_le","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothSelection.lean#L154-L163","doc":"**And such an `N` exists.**  Constructed from the heights, which is the point: the order is\nheights → `N` → degrees, never the other way. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.hlarge_of_pow_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.hlarge_of_pow_le","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothSelection.lean#L136-L152","doc":"**`N` large relative to the heights gives `Γ_m`'s `hlarge`.**  `(H h)^{p+2q} ≤ N` for every\n`h` is the whole condition, and `p ≥ 1` does the rest. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.exists_heights_growing_floor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.exists_heights_growing_floor","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothSelection.lean#L105-L123","doc":"**The floor clause too.**  At `N₀ = 2 ^ F` the selected heights also satisfy\n`rothGammaFull_of_heights`'s `hfloor`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.exists_heights_growing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.exists_heights_growing","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothSelection.lean#L80-L103","doc":"**Two of `Γ_m`'s clauses, from an unbounded supply.**  Given infinitely many admissible\nheights, `m` of them can be chosen from the supply, all beyond an arbitrary floor `N₀`, with\n`H j ^ (2q) ≤ H k ^ p` on consecutive indices.\n\nThat is `rothGammaFull_of_heights`'s `hgrow` and `hH` at once — and taking `N₀ := 2 ^ F` also gives\nits `floor` clause, which is why the floor is a parameter rather than the constant `2`.  Clause 3\nis the one that bites hardest (`RothRealLadder`'s witness needed `H = 1024` at `m = 2` because of\nit), so having it fall out of the same construction is worth the generality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.growSeq_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.growSeq_mono","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothSelection.lean#L67-L78","doc":"**The greedy sequence is monotone.**  Each term is at least its predecessor's `k`-th power,\nand the floor keeps every term at least `1`, so a `k ≥ 1` growth function cannot decrease.\n\nNeeded because `sum_rothDegrees_le` bounds `Σ r_h` using the *smallest* height, and \"smallest\"\nis only `H₀` if the heights increase. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.growSeq_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.growSeq_succ","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothSelection.lean#L61-L65","doc":"Each term outruns the growth function applied to its predecessor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.le_growSeq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.le_growSeq","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothSelection.lean#L52-L59","doc":"The floor is respected at every index — this is what keeps `Γ_m`'s `two_le` clause true past\nthe first term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.growSeq_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.growSeq_mem","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothSelection.lean#L47-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.growSeq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.growSeq","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothSelection.lean#L41-L45","doc":"**The greedy fast-growing selection.**  Each term is chosen from the supply beyond both the\nfloor `N₀` and the growth function applied to its predecessor. ","signatureChunk":0}]}